From def62da2223600917ca2d0667077e90197cc5802 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:19:47 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(sim): read a turning nose path's hidden rest as the
 turned work sees it

A lathe Facing on a grooved bar was refused at the post: the envelope
verdict's hidden-rest half read the groove floor across the spindle
(a scan that never turns the work) and, once turned, 14 mm below the
faced band, as the Facing's own rest. The Profile kinds met the same
far-side reading, then the groove's inner corner a 0.8 nose cannot
reach and the rough's own 0.25 leave.

The app now hands law (f) the spindle a turning nose op's kernel fitted
(VerifyContext::lathe_axis, via turning::Frame::about). With it the
hidden half (stock_sim::scan_turned) reads each hidden top on its
orbit about the spindle, excuses a top outside the axial band the nose
centres travel, excuses a crease the nose (grown by the leave) cannot
touch (the ridge law's own accessibility test), and lets the op's
stock_to_leave stand. Gouge and visible halves, and every mill path,
are unchanged; without a spindle the scan is bit for bit the old one.

Fixes #1408

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
